pgc|a|Belonging to the essence, or that which makes an object, or class of objects, what it is. ; Hence, really existing; existent. ; Important in the highest degree; indispensable to the attainment of an object; indispensably necessary. ; Containing the essence or characteristic portion of a substance, as of a plant; highly rectified; pure; hence, unmixed; as, an essential oil. ; Necessary; indispensable; -- said of those tones which constitute a chord, in distinction from ornamental or passing tones. ; Idiopathic; independent of other diseases.	j:1hxl,69,5;nfe,58,5;eau,56,5;1v3m,51,6;gqn,49,7;22p9,33,3;fd3,31,3;f8h,30,4;k03,28,5;zfo,19,3~gqn,49,7;1v3m,51,6;nfe,58,5;18db,18,5;1gm9,16,5;k03,28,5;eau,56,5;1hxl,69,5;21y4,9,4;2881,3,4	e:b5,60,24;e9a,16,3;2aq,15,3;1oar,12,9;1lgp,5,2;15u7,4,3~b5,60,24;1oar,12,9;e9a,16,3;15u7,4,3;2aq,15,3;1lgp,5,2
